# An X.509 certificate — the PUBLIC document a TLS server presents to every
# client that connects. "BEGIN CERTIFICATE" (no PRIVATE KEY block) = safe.
# Contrast with ../../key-and-cert-containers/client-cert.pem, which pairs a
# cert WITH a private key.
